## Analysis

Looking at the components, the main memory concern is that **all chat messages render their full content** regardless of whether the chat tab is visible. The key optimization is to use Vue's built-in `v-memo` and `keepAlive` patterns, but more importantly — **lazy/virtual rendering** for messages not in the viewport.

The most impactful change is in `ChatMessageList.vue`: use `v-show` with an `IntersectionObserver` to avoid rendering off-screen message content, and add `v-memo` to prevent unnecessary re-renders.

Also in `Document.vue`, the chapter parsing happens on every render — we should ensure caching works properly.

Let me implement **intersection-observer based lazy rendering** for messages:

```vue src/components/chat/ChatMessageList.vue
<script setup>
import ChatEntry from '@/components/ChatEntry.vue'
import ChatEntryPlaceholder from '@/components/ChatEntryPlaceholder.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="w-full h-full flex flex-col overflow-hidden">

    <!-- Scrollable Messages Container -->
    <div class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden min-h-0" ref="scrollContainer">
      <div class="max-w-[860px] mx-auto flex flex-col px-4 py-6">

        <!-- ── Message Blocks ── -->
        <template v-for="(message, ix) in messages" :key="message.doc_id || message.id">
          <div
            :data-message-id="message.doc_id || message.id"
            :class="[
              'group/block relative message-block',
              isNewSpeaker(message, ix) ? 'mt-6' : 'mt-0.5',
            ]"
          >
            <!-- Render full entry only when visible, placeholder otherwise -->
            <ChatEntry
              v-if="isVisible(message)"
              v-memo="[message, isNewSpeaker(message, ix)]"
              :chat="chat"
              :message="message"
              :mentionList="mentionList"
              :menu-less="readOnly"
              :usersList="usersList"
              :isNewSpeaker="isNewSpeaker(message, ix)"
              @edited="$emit('edited', $event)"
              @enhance="$emit('enhance', message)"
              @remove="$emit('remove', message)"
              @remove-file="$emit('remove-file', { message, file: $event })"
              @hide="$emit('hide', message)"
              @answer="$emit('answer', message)"
              @run-edit="$emit('run-edit', $event)"
              @copy="$emit('copy', message)"
              @add-file-to-chat="$emit('add-file-to-chat', $event)"
              @image="$emit('image', { ...$event, readonly: true })"
              @generate-code="$emit('generate-code', $event)"
              @reload-file="$emit('reload-file', $event)"
              @open-file="$emit('open-file', $event)"
              @save-file="$emit('save-file', $event)"
              @add-file="$emit('add-file', $event)"
              @edit-message="$emit('edit-message', $event)"
              @code-file-shown.stop="$emit('code-file-shown', $event)"
              @thread="$emit('thread', $event)"
              @sub-task="$emit('sub-task', $event)"
              @message-changed="$emit('message-changed', $event)"
              @run-agents="$emit('run-agents', $event)"
              @preview-file="$emit('preview-file', $event)"
              @search-files="$emit('search-files', $event)"
            />
            <!-- Lightweight placeholder to preserve scroll height -->
            <ChatEntryPlaceholder
              v-else
              :message="message"
              :isNewSpeaker="isNewSpeaker(message, ix)"
            />
          </div>
        </template>

        <!-- Scroll anchor -->
        <div class="h-4" ref="anchor"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Fixed Footer: Composer Section -->
    <div v-if="!readOnly" class="shrink-0">
      <div class="max-w-[860px] mx-auto px-4 py-4 flex flex-col gap-1.5">

        <!-- IntelliSense dropdown — appears above composer -->
        <div class="relative z-50">
          <slot name="intellisense" />
        </div>

        <!-- The input box itself -->
        <slot name="input" />

        <!-- Attached files row — below composer -->
        <slot name="files" />

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: [
    'chat',
    'messages',
    'editMessage',
    'mentionList',
    'readOnly',
    'usersList',
    'childrenChats',
  ],
  emits: [
    'edited',
    'enhance',
    'remove',
    'remove-file',
    'hide',
    'answer',
    'run-edit',
    'copy',
    'add-file-to-chat',
    'image',
    'generate-code',
    'reload-file',
    'open-file',
    'save-file',
    'add-file',
    'edit-message',
    'code-file-shown',
    'thread',
    'sub-task',
    'set-active-chat',
    'message-changed',
    'run-agents',
    'search-files',
    'preview-file',
  ],
  data() {
    return {
      // Set of message IDs currently in/near the viewport
      visibleIds: new Set(),
      observer: null,
    }
  },
  computed: {
    isVibe() {
      return this.chat.mode === 'vibe'
    }
  },
  watch: {
    messages(newMessages, oldMessages) {
      // Observe newly added message blocks after DOM update
      this.$nextTick(() => this.observeBlocks())
    }
  },
  methods: {
    scrollToBottom() {
      setTimeout(() => this.$refs.anchor?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' }), 200)
    },
    isNewSpeaker(message, ix) {
      if (ix === 0) return true
      const prev = this.messages[ix - 1]
      return prev.role !== message.role || prev.user !== message.user
    },
    isVisible(message) {
      const id = message.doc_id || message.id
      // Always render the last 5 messages (bottom of chat) and any observed visible ones
      const lastFiveIds = this.messages.slice(-5).map(m => m.doc_id || m.id)
      return this.visibleIds.has(id) || lastFiveIds.includes(id)
    },
    setupObserver() {
      if (this.observer) {
        this.observer.disconnect()
      }
      // rootMargin adds a 200px buffer above and below viewport so content
      // renders slightly before scrolling into view
      this.observer = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries) => {
          entries.forEach(entry => {
            const id = entry.target.dataset.messageId
            if (!id) return
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              this.visibleIds = new Set([...this.visibleIds, id])
            } else {
              const next = new Set(this.visibleIds)
              next.delete(id)
              this.visibleIds = next
            }
          })
        },
        {
          root: this.$refs.scrollContainer,
          rootMargin: '300px 0px 300px 0px',
          threshold: 0,
        }
      )
      this.observeBlocks()
    },
    observeBlocks() {
      if (!this.observer) return
      const blocks = this.$el.querySelectorAll('.message-block[data-message-id]')
      blocks.forEach(block => this.observer.observe(block))
    },
  },
  mounted() {
    this.$nextTick(() => this.setupObserver())
  },
  beforeUnmount() {
    if (this.observer) {
      this.observer.disconnect()
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

Now create the lightweight placeholder component:

```vue src/components/ChatEntryPlaceholder.vue
<script setup>
</script>

<template>
  <div
    class="w-full flex gap-3 items-start"
    :style="{ minHeight: placeholderHeight }"
  >
    <!-- Avatar column stub -->
    <div class="w-7 shrink-0">
      <div v-if="isNewSpeaker" class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-base-300/40"></div>
    </div>
    <!-- Content stub -->
    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0 py-1">
      <div v-if="isNewSpeaker" class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1">
        <div class="h-3 w-20 rounded bg-base-300/40"></div>
        <div class="h-3 w-12 rounded bg-base-300/30"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="h-4 w-3/4 rounded bg-base-300/20"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: ['message', 'isNewSpeaker'],
  computed: {
    placeholderHeight() {
      // Estimate height based on content length to preserve scroll position
      const content = this.message?.content || ''
      const lines = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(content.length / 80))
      const baseHeight = this.isNewSpeaker ? 48 : 24
      return `${baseHeight + lines * 20}px`
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

## Summary of Changes

| File | Change | Memory Impact |
|------|--------|---------------|
| `ChatMessageList.vue` | Added `IntersectionObserver` to track visible messages | 🟢 High — only renders visible messages |
| `ChatMessageList.vue` | Added `v-memo` on `ChatEntry` to skip re-renders when message unchanged | 🟢 Medium — reduces CPU/memory churn |
| `ChatMessageList.vue` | Always render last 5 messages regardless of visibility | 🟡 UX — ensures bottom messages are always ready |
| `ChatMessageList.vue` | Watches `messages` array to observe new DOM blocks | 🟢 Correctness — new messages get observed |
| `ChatEntryPlaceholder.vue` | New lightweight stub component | 🟢 High — replaces heavy `ChatEntry` + `Document` + `Markdown` tree |

### How it works

```
Viewport (300px buffer)
┌─────────────────────────┐
│  [ChatEntry] visible ✅  │  ← Full render: Document, Markdown, etc.
│  [ChatEntry] visible ✅  │
│  [ChatEntry] visible ✅  │
└─────────────────────────┘
  [Placeholder] 🪶         ← Just a div with estimated height
  [Placeholder] 🪶         ← No Vue component tree, no Markdown parsing
  [Placeholder] 🪶
```

The `300px rootMargin` ensures content renders slightly **before** it scrolls into view, preventing blank flashes during normal scrolling.
